  "summary": "Held the entire episode. Price moved favorably almost immediately and built to large gains (peaking near +65pts around t=32m), with several sharp pullbacks along the way (e.g. +43->+3.75 at t=8m, +51->+27 at t=41-42m) that each recovered before going negative. None of these pullbacks ever approached breakeven or reversed the entry's thesis -- they read as normal volatility/consolidation within a working trade, not wrong-direction action, so I never saw a bail signal. Next time I'd watch for a pullback that actually crosses back toward zero (not just a high giveback % of a small recent leg) as the real wrong-direction tell, since giveback% alone was noisy and misleading on its own several times here."
